WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.476
Auto starts at Low, to stay smooth. Check this device finds out how much more this

00:00:07.476 --> 00:00:08.552
one can hold.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.251
It rides a test world off screen, level by level from the top, about thirty seconds

00:00:15.251 --> 00:00:17.748
each, and shows what each level held.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:28.066
It stops at the first level that holds the display's rate, says so, and keeps the

00:00:28.066 --> 00:00:31.532
result on this device. A fixed level stays as chosen.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:40.931
Auto then starts there. A race opens at Medium, where this check found it smooth,

00:00:40.931 --> 00:00:42.119
instead of Low.

00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:51.846
The check's result, from a phone to the full screen.

00:00:59.361 --> 00:01:04.270
Stop the check, or hide the tab, and its renderer is let go: nothing more is drawn

00:01:04.270 --> 00:01:05.767
and nothing is kept.

00:01:09.685 --> 00:01:14.288
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:14.633 --> 00:01:19.145
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:20.816
every hill and interval.

00:01:21.161 --> 00:01:26.339
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:26.339 --> 00:01:31.787
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:01:31.787 --> 00:01:34.777
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:01:35.123 --> 00:01:37.615
A custom workout lives under Profile.
